# Altanak's "{1}{G}, Discard this card: Return target land card from your graveyard to the battlefield tapped" works from
# the hand (CR 602.2) and its target is a land card in YOUR graveyard (CR 115.1): Bot2's Strip Mine, in Bot2's graveyard, is
# refused while Bot1's Forest, put there by that Strip Mine, is taken. Ruby + Jet cannot pay the {G}; adding Emerald can,
# leaving one mana (the cost is {1}{G}, not more). The land comes back tapped. On turn 5, with the Moxen and the Forest
# untapped to pay, the second Altanak's ability is refused: the only card left in Bot1's graveyard is the discarded Altanak,
# a creature card, not a land card, so there is no legal target (CR 602.2b, 601.2c).

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Mox Emerald
Altanak, the Thrice-Called
Altanak, the Thrice-Called
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Strip Mine
Island x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Strip Mine.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Strip Mine.Activate(Bot1.Battlefield.Forest; Ability: Destroy)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
! Bot1.Hand.Altanak, the Thrice-Called.Activate(Mana: short)
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
! Bot1.Hand.Altanak, the Thrice-Called.Activate(Bot2.Graveyard.Strip Mine)
Bot1.Hand.Altanak, the Thrice-Called.Activate(Bot1.Graveyard.Forest; Spend: B, G)
Bot1.Pass
? Bot1.Mana = {R}
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Tapped = true
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
! Bot1.Hand.Altanak, the Thrice-Called.Activate(Bot1.Graveyard.Altanak, the Thrice-Called)
! Bot1.Hand.Altanak, the Thrice-Called.Activate
[T5 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Tapped = false
Bot1.Graveyard = Altanak, the Thrice-Called
Bot2.Graveyard = Strip Mine
Bot1.Hand = Altanak, the Thrice-Called; Island; Island; Island
